# The dependencies this repository asks for, edited by hand (TODO S209, owner 23 Nov 2026).
#
# requirements.txt is GENERATED from this file and pins every package, the
# dependencies of these included, so Streamlit Cloud, CI and a Windows machine
# install the same set. Never edit requirements.txt by hand. After changing this
# file, regenerate it and commit both:
#
#     uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.14 -o requirements.txt
#
# Python 3.14 is what Streamlit Cloud runs (deploy log, 22 Nov 2026: 3.14.10) and
# what .python-version gives CI. --universal writes one file for Linux, macOS and
# Windows, with markers where they differ. The first compile added
# --exclude-newer 2026-11-22T17:37:00Z, the moment of production's last full
# install, so its 39 pins equal what production already ran; drop that flag, or
# move the date, to take newer releases. 23 Nov 2026: recompiled without it for
# numpy 2.5.5 (owner, Dependabot #642); uv kept every other pin. pyarrow went
# to 26.0.1 with it (#641) and back to 24.0.0 the same day: see the pyarrow note.
#
# Ranges below stay ranges here on purpose (boto3); requirements.txt pins
# the version they resolve to.

# Pinned, not floated. `streamlit>=1.35.0` let Streamlit Cloud install a
# different FRONTEND on any reboot with no commit in this repository, and the
# frontend is where the Configuration sliders rendered at their minimum.
# Production confirmed 1.63.0 is what this deployment already resolves to, so
# this pin changes nothing today and stops the next silent swap. To upgrade:
# bump here, let V1 Production QA verify against the live app, then keep it.
# 15 Nov 2026: 1.66.1 -> 1.67.0 (owner: "we should be using latest"). Checked
# locally on both versions: 56 screens of six pages at 1400 and 390 px, page text
# identical, 0 exceptions, one table's columns a few pixels apart; suite passed.
streamlit==1.67.0
# The numeric stack and the data clients are pinned for the same reason as
# streamlit: a floor like `pandas>=2.0.0` let every container boot pick up
# whatever was newest that day, while CI had only ever tested one version.
# These are the versions the full suite passed on (2026-09-25). pandas 3 and
# numpy 2 change dtype and copy semantics the engine depends on, and a floor
# of 2.0.0 / 1.24.0 claimed support for versions nothing ever ran. Dependabot
# (monthly, increase-if-necessary) opens a PR for each new release; bump
# deliberately and let CI plus V1 Production QA confirm it.
pandas==3.1.1
numpy==2.5.5
# scikit-learn was declared here and imported NOWHERE -- `grep -rn sklearn`
# across the repository returns this line and nothing else. Carrying it cost
# the cold start a ~30 MB wheel plus joblib and threadpoolctl on every container
# boot, for nothing. scipy went the same way on
# 2026-09-25: its only user was an Equal Risk Contribution optimiser nothing
# in the app could reach.
requests==2.34.2
# Pinned to the exact version, not capped below a range.
#
# pyarrow 25.0.1 segfaults (apache/arrow#50471) and Streamlit Cloud knows it:
# every boot it detected 25.0.1, uninstalled it and installed 24.0.0 itself,
# so the float was buying no newer version anyway -- only an uninstall and a
# reinstall on the critical path of every cold start.
#
# `pyarrow<25` would have been a permanent ceiling for a temporary bug, and
# nothing would ever have prompted a re-look. An exact pin is a line with a
# reason and a way out: when arrow#50471 closes, bump this deliberately and
# let the QA run confirm it.
#
# 7 Nov 2026: bumped to 26.0.0 and back the same evening. Streamlit Cloud's
# boot log: "Detected pyarrow 26.0.0 (known segfault, apache/arrow#50471).
# Replacing with pyarrow<25." It treats every version from 25 as bad, so
# production ran 24 anyway; the pin says what production runs. Checked with
# streamlit 1.66.1, pandas 3.1.0, numpy 2.5.4: suite, audit baseline and
# parity unchanged.
#
# 23 Nov 2026: the same again. #645 pinned 26.0.1 (owner's yes on Dependabot
# #641, audit baseline IDENTICAL to 24.0.0); the first boot after it logged
# "Detected pyarrow 26.0.1 (known segfault, apache/arrow#50471). Replacing with
# pyarrow<25." Back to 24.0.0, and dependabot.yml now ignores pyarrow 25+, so
# it stops proposing a version production refuses. Way out unchanged: when
# Streamlit Cloud stops replacing it, lift the ignore and bump here.
pyarrow==24.0.0
# S3-compatible Cloudflare R2 archive adapter. Left as a range on purpose:
# boto3 releases almost daily, its S3 API is stable within a major, and the
# R2 read-path gate re-runs on main whenever this file changes.
boto3>=1.35.0,<2

# Eight test files parse workflow YAML and have always imported this, while
# requirements.txt never declared it: it was present only as an optional extra
# of conan, uvicorn, watchdog, pytest and starlette. The r2-focused job
# installs requirements.txt alone, so PR #506 went red with
# "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'yaml'" while every other job and the
# full local suite passed (owner, 11 Nov 2026, S121). Declared, not removed:
# it is already installed in every environment this runs in, so saying so
# costs nothing and makes true what the tests assume. Pinned to what this
# container resolves to today, as with the rest of the file.
PyYAML==6.0.3

